  "parsed_answer": "Finasteride treats hair loss by **inhibiting the enzyme 5-alpha-reductase type II**, which normally converts **testosterone into dihydrotestosterone (DHT)**.\n\n### Why that matters\n- **DHT** is a key hormone involved in **androgenetic alopecia** (male-pattern hair loss).\n- In susceptible hair follicles, DHT causes **follicle miniaturization**, making hairs grow back thinner and shorter over time.\n\n### Effect of finasteride\nBy lowering DHT levels in the scalp and bloodstream, finasteride:\n- **slows hair loss**\n- may **promote some regrowth**\n- helps **preserve existing hair**\n\nIt does **not** permanently cure hair loss; its benefits generally continue only while the medication is being taken.",
